---
interface Props {kind:'lexical'|'vectors'}
const {kind}=Astro.props;
---
<search-lab class="lab wide" data-kind={kind} aria-label={kind==='lexical'?'Find catalogue products by terms':'Filter the nearest products'}>
 <div class="lab-heading"><span class="eyebrow">Interactive experiment</span><span class="lab-number">{kind==='lexical'?'01':'02'}</span></div>
 <h3>{kind==='lexical'?'Which products do the term lists find?':'When does the stock filter run?'}</h3>
 <div class="lab-introduction">{kind==='lexical'?<><p>Five catalogue titles are indexed. The analyser groups Unicode letters and digits, lowercases them, and treats punctuation as a separator. It does not stem words, remove accents, or add synonyms. Search uses visible segments. Every catalogue update here is also delivered to and accepted by the search engine into its indexing buffer. Refresh opens that accepted version for search; it does not fetch the catalogue. Each matched query term adds 1 divided by the number of searchable titles containing that term to the score.</p><p class="try-this">Search for <strong>blue mug</strong> with all terms, then any term. Rename and restock the mug, and compare the catalogue with search before and after <strong>Refresh</strong>. <strong>Merge segments</strong> should preserve the answer.</p></>:<><p>These are the same five titles in their original state. We've assigned two coordinates by hand: blue colour and mug-like shape. Every distance is calculated exactly. The question is which two in-stock products a nearest-neighbour query returns.</p><p class="try-this">For <strong>Blue mug</strong>, choose <strong>Take two, then filter</strong>. Both nearest products are out of stock. Choose <strong>Filter, then take two</strong> to find two eligible products instead.</p></>}</div>
 <div class="lab-controls"><p class="lab-area-label">Controls</p>{kind==='lexical'?<><div class="control-line"><label>Query <input data-query type="text" value="blue mug" maxlength="80" /></label><label>Matching <select data-mode><option value="all">All terms (AND)</option><option value="any">Any term (OR)</option></select></label><label><input data-stock type="checkbox" /> In stock only</label></div><div class="control-line"><button data-action="update">Rename &amp; restock mug</button><button data-action="refresh">Refresh</button><button data-action="merge">Merge segments</button><button data-action="reset">Reset</button></div></>:<div class="control-line"><label>Query point <select data-vector-query><option>Blue mug</option><option>White mug</option><option>Blue bowl</option></select></label><label>Order <select data-order><option value="early">Filter, then take two</option><option value="late">Take two, then filter</option></select></label></div>}</div>
 <div class="lab-output paper-surface"><p class="lab-area-label">Result <span>{kind==='lexical'?'Terms, searchable versions, and ranked matches':'Exact distances and eligible results'}</span></p><div data-view></div><p data-status class="lab-explanation" role="status" aria-live="polite" aria-atomic="true"></p></div>
 <details class="model-note"><summary>What this model leaves out</summary>{kind==='lexical'?<p>Only titles are tokenised. A matched term contributes 1 divided by the number of visible titles containing it; scores are summed. This is an invented ranking rule, not BM25. Delivery from the catalogue to the search engine succeeds immediately; there is no delivery queue or failure. Refresh is manual and each nonempty refresh creates one segment from the already accepted indexing buffer. Merge rewrites every live document. Real engines add postings compression, term frequencies, positions, field lengths, shard coordination, and more complex merges. No durability or timing is simulated.</p>:<p>Coordinates are hand-assigned, not produced by an embedding model. Distances are Euclidean in two dimensions, and all five are computed before either ordering is applied. The diagram tests the effect of truncating a candidate list before filtering. It does not implement or benchmark HNSW, IVFFlat, approximate recall, or a production embedding's relevance.</p>}</details>
 <noscript><p>JavaScript enables the controls. The article explains the results: all-term search intersects term lists, refresh exposes updates already accepted by search, and filtering a truncated list can leave too few eligible results.</p></noscript>
</search-lab>
<script>
 import {createSearchState,searchStep,searchLexical,searchVectors} from '../../lib/explainers/search-model.mjs';
 const searchEscape=(value:any)=>String(value).replace(/[&<>"']/g,c=>({'&':'&amp;','<':'&lt;','>':'&gt;','"':'&quot;',"'":'&#39;'}[c]!));
 class SearchLab extends HTMLElement{
 connectedCallback(){
  let state=createSearchState();const kind=this.dataset.kind;
  const draw=()=>{
   const view=this.querySelector('[data-view]')!;let status='';
   if(kind==='lexical'){
    const query=(this.querySelector('[data-query]') as HTMLInputElement).value,mode=(this.querySelector('[data-mode]') as HTMLSelectElement).value,stock=(this.querySelector('[data-stock]') as HTMLInputElement).checked;
    const r=searchLexical(state,query,mode,stock);
    view.innerHTML=`<div class="search-grid"><div><h4>Term → product IDs</h4>${r.postings.length?r.postings.map((p:any)=>`<p><b>${searchEscape(p.term)}</b> → ${p.ids.join(', ')||'no postings'}</p>`).join(''):'<p>No query terms</p>'}<p>${r.entries} posting entries in these lists</p><h4>Segments</h4>${state.segments.map((s:any)=>`<p>Segment ${s.number}: ${s.docs.map((d:any)=>`#${d.id} v${d.version}${state.deleted.includes(`${d.id}:${d.version}`)?' (deleted)':''}`).join(', ')}</p>`).join('')}<h4>Accepted indexing buffer</h4>${state.pending.length?state.pending.map((d:any)=>`<p>#${d.id} ${d.title} · stock ${d.stock} · v${d.version}<br>Accepted by search; waiting to become searchable</p>`).join(''):'<p>No accepted update waiting</p>'}</div><div><h4>Ranked search results</h4>${r.results.length?r.results.map((d:any)=>`<p><b>#${d.id} ${d.title}</b><span>Score ${d.score.toFixed(2)} · stock ${d.stock} · v${d.version}</span></p>`).join(''):'<p>No matching products</p>'}</div></div><h4>Catalogue and searchable titles</h4><div class="search-table"><table><thead><tr><th>Product</th><th>Catalogue now</th><th>Search can see</th></tr></thead><tbody>${state.source.map((d:any)=>{const visible=r.docs.find((p:any)=>p.id===d.id)!;return `<tr><td>#${d.id}</td><td>${d.title}<br>stock ${d.stock} · v${d.version}</td><td>${visible.title}<br>stock ${visible.stock} · v${visible.version}</td></tr>`;}).join('')}</tbody></table></div>`;
    (this.querySelector('[data-action="update"]') as HTMLButtonElement).disabled=state.pending.length>0;
    (this.querySelector('[data-action="merge"]') as HTMLButtonElement).disabled=state.segments.length<2;
    status=`${r.results.length} matching ${r.results.length===1?'product':'products'}. ${state.message}`;
   }else{
    const q=(this.querySelector('[data-vector-query]') as HTMLSelectElement).value,early=(this.querySelector('[data-order]') as HTMLSelectElement).value==='early',r=searchVectors(q,early);
    view.innerHTML=`<div class="search-grid"><svg viewBox="0 0 310 250" role="img" aria-label="Products plotted by blue colour and mug-like shape; product IDs correspond to the distance list"><path d="M40 20V205H280" fill="none" stroke="currentColor"/><text x="42" y="16" font-size="11">More mug-like ↑</text><text x="145" y="240" font-size="11">More blue →</text>${r.all.map((d:any)=>`<circle cx="${40+d.vector[0]*230}" cy="${205-d.vector[1]*160}" r="5" fill="${d.stock?'var(--teal)':'var(--coral)'}"/><text x="${35+d.vector[0]*230}" y="${222-d.vector[1]*160}" font-size="12">${d.id}</text>`).join('')}<path d="M${40+r.query[0]*230-7} ${205-r.query[1]*160}h14m-7 -7v14" stroke="var(--color-text)" stroke-width="2"/><text x="180" y="28" font-size="11">+ Query</text></svg><div><h4>All exact distances</h4>${r.all.map((d:any)=>`<p><b>#${d.id} ${d.title}</b><span>${d.distance.toFixed(3)} · ${d.stock?'in stock':'out of stock'}${r.candidates.some((p:any)=>p.id===d.id)?' · selected before final check':''}</span></p>`).join('')}</div></div><h4>Final in-stock results (${r.results.length} of requested 2)</h4><p>${r.results.length?r.results.map((d:any)=>`#${d.id} ${d.title}`).join(' · '):'None'}</p>`;
    status=`Calculated all ${r.distances} distances. ${early?'Discarded out-of-stock products before taking the nearest two.':'Took the nearest two first, then discarded out-of-stock products without backfilling.'} Returned ${r.results.length} products.`;
   }
   this.querySelector('[data-status]')!.textContent=status;
  };
  this.addEventListener('input',draw);this.addEventListener('change',draw);
  this.addEventListener('click',event=>{const b=(event.target as HTMLElement).closest<HTMLButtonElement>('button[data-action]');if(!b)return;const type=b.dataset.action!;if(type==='reset'){state=createSearchState();(this.querySelector('[data-query]') as HTMLInputElement).value='blue mug';(this.querySelector('[data-mode]') as HTMLSelectElement).value='all';(this.querySelector('[data-stock]') as HTMLInputElement).checked=false;}else state=searchStep(state,type);draw();});draw();
 }
 }
 if(!customElements.get('search-lab'))customElements.define('search-lab',SearchLab);
</script>
<style>
 .lab input[type="text"]{font:inherit;border:1px solid var(--control);border-radius:6px;padding:.6rem;max-width:100%;width:11rem;background:var(--color-surface);color:var(--color-text);}
 [data-view] :global(h4){font-size:.85rem;margin:1rem 0 .5rem;}
 [data-view] :global(p){font-size:.8rem;line-height:1.65;padding:.4rem 0;margin:.3rem 0;border-bottom:1px solid var(--color-rule);overflow-wrap:anywhere;}
 [data-view] :global(p span){display:block;}
 [data-view] :global(.search-grid){display:grid;grid-template-columns:1fr 1fr;gap:1.5rem;}
 [data-view] :global(.search-table){overflow-x:auto;}
 [data-view] :global(table){width:100%;border-collapse:collapse;font:.77rem/1.6 var(--font-sans);min-width:350px;}
 [data-view] :global(th),[data-view] :global(td){padding:.6rem .4rem;border-bottom:1px solid var(--color-rule-strong);text-align:left;vertical-align:top;}
 [data-view] :global(svg){width:100%;height:auto;align-self:center;color:var(--color-text);}
 [data-view] :global(svg text){fill:currentColor;}
 @media(max-width:650px){[data-view] :global(.search-grid){grid-template-columns:1fr;gap:.5rem;}}
</style>
